    biography: `Professor Nordin received his BS in Physics from BYU in 1984, MS in Physics from UCLA in 1986, and PhD in Electrical Engineering from USC in 1992. From 1984-1992, he worked at Hughes Aircraft Company in various groups including Radar Systems, Electro-optical and Data Systems, and Hughes Research Laboratory.

From 1992-2005, he was at University of Alabama in Huntsville as Assistant, Associate, and Full Professor. He founded and directed the Nano and Micro Devices Center, leading 10-15 PhD students and 5-8 full-time staff. He created a 7,600 sq. ft. cleanroom facility for research in photonics, MEMS, microfluidics, and sensors. He joined BYU as Full Professor in 2005.

He has led large research programs as principal investigator on grants totaling $18M. Awards include NSF CAREER award (1996), UAH Outstanding Researcher Award (1998-1999, 1999-2000), and UAH Foundation Award for Research and Creative Achievement (2000).`,
